\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 What went into his success:
\f0\b0  Kai built an audience around recognizable reactions and group chemistry, then expanded into progressively more ambitious productions. Celebrity collaborations made individual streams newsworthy. Long marathons gave viewers recurring reasons to check back. Clips spread the funniest moments to people who weren't watching live.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 The crucial transformation was from 
\f7\i watching Kai do something
\f0\i0  to 
\f7\i following whatever happens in Kai's world
\f0\i0 .\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 The special ingredient:
\f0\b0  An ensemble of recurring characters, relationships, jokes, and unpredictable events. The viewers are following a social universe, not just a single host.\cf0 \cb1 \

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 What transfers:
\f0\b0  Recurring guests, running jokes, episodic events, and clip-friendly moments. What doesn't transfer easily is the celebrity network, production spending, or preexisting audience.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <$Scr_H::3>
\f8\b\fs40 Case study: Ludwig Ahgren \'97 making a stream feel like an event\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0\fs28 Ludwig's landmark 2021 subathon ran for roughly 31 days. Subscribers added time to a countdown, making the audience partly responsible for how long the broadcast continued. It generated 282,191 subscriptions and helped popularize the format. \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs24 \cf0 {\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename favicons}\picw32\pich32\picwgoal640\pichgoal640\pngblip }}\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs16 \cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 The Loadout\cf8 \cb1 \strokec8 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf8 \cb7 +1\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Before that event, Ludwig already had an audience from gaming, commentary, tournaments, and gameshow-style streams. The subathon accelerated an existing career rather than creating one from nothing.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 His larger lesson is that 
\f3\b formats can be as important as personality
\f0\b0 .\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 A seemingly ordinary streamer can become much more interesting when viewers understand an overarching objective: finishing a challenge, reaching a milestone, deciding a result, or watching an experiment unfold.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Ludwig also developed the organizational ability to produce events and collaborate with other creators. That's a different skill from being entertaining on camera\'97and a significant part of his longer-term success. \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

