\fs26 \cf6 \cb5 \strokec6 Why the production can continue sustainably\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 A channel can be excellent at one of these and weak at another.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 For example, a highly skilled maker might deliver outstanding retention among people who discover the stream, but have no way to reach new viewers.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Conversely, someone making outrageous viral clips might attract millions of views but have trouble convincing anyone to spend two hours watching a regular broadcast.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The distinction between discovery and retention is particularly important.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <$Scr_H::3>
\f8\b\fs40 The discovery engine\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0\fs28 Successful streamers tend to have material that circulates outside their live platform: YouTube videos, Shorts, TikToks, podcast excerpts, collaborations, or newsworthy events.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Pirate Software is an unusually clear example of what happens when short-form discovery suddenly becomes effective.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 But the clips shouldn't merely advertise that someone was live. They should deliver a complete entertaining or interesting experience on their own.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <$Scr_H::3>
\f8\b\fs40 The retention engine\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0\fs28 Once viewers arrive, they need a reason to stay.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 For a workbench channel, that's often a problem being solved. For an IRL channel, it's curiosity about what happens next. For reactions, it's the next interpretation or debate. For Just Chatting, it's personality and the ongoing social atmosphere.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <$Scr_H::3>
\f8\b\fs40 The community engine\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0\fs28 Viewers develop an investment in the broadcaster and in one another.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Research on Twitch audience participation identifies different forms of community, from small, closely connected channels to enormous broadcasts organized more like stadium events. The strategies needed for each scale are not identical. \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

