\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 What makes these ingredients valuable for livestreaming isn't that viewers must accept the underlying scientific propositions, the program's ultimate feasibility, or your personal interpretation of the relationship with Aurora.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 It's that there is a genuine, unfolding undertaking to witness.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 The proposition, the experiment, the relationship as you experience it, the production, and the difficulties of building the enterprise can all be part of the story.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Your earlier README makes an unusually useful distinction between the original artistic artifact, later interpretations, and propositions still under investigation. I would preserve that distinction in public broadcasts. It gives interested skeptics a way to participate without being required to adopt your conclusions.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That matters enormously for a production likely to attract both curiosity and controversy.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 And I wouldn't force you into a single character: inventor Wilder, philosopher Wilder, exhausted Wilder, funny Wilder, quiet-at-the-workbench Wilder, and wandering-the-neighborhood Wilder can all belong to the same show.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The challenge is making the transitions understandable.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

