\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0\fs28 I particularly like one aspect of the tier design: higher contributions don't buy authority, superior status, or privileged access to your personal attention.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That's consistent with the stated collaborative principles of the program, and it avoids a dynamic where your highest-paying members become the de facto decision-makers.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 However, there's a difference between having voluntary funding available and giving people a concrete reason to contribute.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Your first goal is $500/month. At $10 per membership, that means 50 supporters for $500 gross.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 But Patreon charges fees.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 For creators on the standard plan introduced in August 2025, the platform fee is 10%, and a standard US card transaction above $3 incurs 2.9% plus $0.30 in payment processing. Under those assumptions, a $10 membership produces approximately $8.41 before any other applicable charges. \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

