\f0\fs28 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 So, if you mean $500 in money available to sustain the undertaking, roughly 60 supporters is a better starting target than 50 under those assumptions.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 And even 60 supporters is not something I'd expect immediately from a dormant YouTube channel. Your 2,700 subscribers represent historical interest, not necessarily an active membership prospect pool.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 My suggestion would be to make Patreon support a tangible continuing experiment:\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 People can see what happened during the month, what was built or learned, what remains unresolved, and what resources would help.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That is different from promising that a contribution will advance world peace in some direct, measurable proportion.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 Ask people to fund the opportunity to do the work\'97not to pay for certainty about its ultimate conclusions.
