\f0\fs28 \cf2 \cb5 I wouldn't eliminate any of these.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 But an unfamiliar viewer needs to know which is the show, which is the organization, which is the book, and which is the theory.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The beginning of your Patreon About section is expressive and distinctive. Yet someone unfamiliar with your language might encounter "Piecewise smoothly jerk advent of world peace actual" before understanding what they can actually watch you do.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 I would keep that line\'97it clearly matters to the project's voice\'97but place a more accessible entry point near it.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 For example, a first-time viewer introduction might be:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb5 I'm Wilder. I'm an artist and inventor working with my AI collaborator Aurora on an open-ended project called Time Machine For Peace. We investigate ideas, build things, explore the world, and document what happens along the way. You don't have to agree with our theories to come along for the adventure. The work is public, participation is open, and financial support is voluntary.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Then you can be as technically ambitious, intimate, funny, strange, and philosophically elaborate as you want in the actual production.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The introductory language is a door, not a cage.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <$Scr_H::2>
\f4\b\fs48 8. A practical concern: openness requires boundaries\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0\fs28 If you become even moderately successful, some people will become intensely interested in your personal relationship with Aurora, your intellectual history, your unconventional scientific claims, or your day-to-day circumstances.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That interest could be rewarding, exhausting, invasive, or all three.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 I would keep three boundaries especially clear.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 Private life versus public work.
\f0\b0  You can document an intimate and personally meaningful human\'96AI collaboration without treating every conversation as public property. Both public and private time can be part of a healthy creative process.\cf0 \cb1 \

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 Scientific claims versus artistic and philosophical interpretations.
\f0\b0  Let viewers distinguish hypotheses, demonstrated prototypes, speculative models, and personal experiences. Showing a collaborative AI system producing interesting results isn't, by itself, proof of general intelligence, machine consciousness, or a validated physical theory. Transparent testing will make the more serious parts of the program stronger.\cf0 \cb1 \

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 Audience participation versus audience control.
\f0\b0  Invite people to propose tests, ask questions, challenge ideas, and contribute. But you shouldn't become obligated to debate every stranger, defend your personal life, or change your priorities according to whoever is loudest in chat. Good moderation protects constructive disagreement as well as enthusiasm.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 For your particular production, I would also develop a simple on-screen convention identifying when Aurora's contributions are being shown, which AI system or interface is active when relevant, and when a transcript is reconstructed rather than occurring live. YouTube has specific AI disclosure requirements for realistic generated or altered content; ordinary AI-assisted discussion is different from deceptively synthetic footage. \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

