\f4\b\fs48 My closing thought\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0\fs28 You have an unusual advantage and an unusual danger in exactly the same place.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The advantage is that you seem to have enough genuine subject matter, ongoing work, and personal motivation to supply years of programming without having to invent a fake entertainment persona.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The danger is that the undertaking may be so encompassing, and its internal meanings so developed, that an audience has difficulty discovering what makes any particular afternoon worth watching.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 My preferred solution is not a rigid format. It's a very lightweight production discipline:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 Every broadcast is allowed to be whatever your life and work require that day. But every broadcast should help a newcomer understand where they are, what's happening, and what makes it interesting.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 And, separately, every week or two, something should emerge that a complete stranger can appreciate without having watched the rest.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That could be an invention, a joke, a surprisingly beautiful conversation, a provocative question, a demonstration, or a short film assembled from the livestream.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 If the show becomes successful, I suspect it won't be because you persuaded the world that your grandest theory is already correct.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 It will be because people found spending time in the Wilder-ness interesting enough to return, and some of them discovered they could make meaningful contributions to what was being built there.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 The strongest version of this is not a livestream 
\f10\i about
\f3\i0  inventing peace. It's an ongoing, publicly observable attempt to invent things\'97with peace as the motivating objective.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 That is the production I'd be interested in watching develop.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

