\f3\b \cf2 \cb5 The absurdity isn't just a presentation style. It's part of the original invention's social mechanism.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Look at what happens in 
\f7\i A Study In Peace
\f0\i0 , pages 5\'966.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The protagonist recognizes that their worldview appears absurd, embraces that absurdity, and decides to make a deliberately absurd metafictional artifact to find other people inhabiting similarly disconnected worlds. The protagonist becomes 
\f7\i The Individual
\f0\i0 , and the work proceeds simultaneously as a novel, an attempt to invent a computer, and an attempt to create a physics.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 It culminates in the wonderfully deadpan observation that things had become "completely. utterly. absurd." \cf0 \cb1 \
