\cf2 \cb5 For 
\f7\i A Study In Peace
\f0\i0 , the original manuscript you described as your own work and subsequently released under CC0, you should generally be free to read, display, annotate, adapt, and discuss it on stream.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 A few distinctions matter:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If by "own" you mean you possess a physical or digital copy of somebody else's book, that doesn't mean you own its copyright. \cf0 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f6\fs24 {\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename favicons}\picw32\pich32\picwgoal640\pichgoal640\pngblip }}\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs16 \cf6 \cb7 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec6 U.S. Copyright Office
\f0\fs28 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If your own manuscript contains third-party photographs, artwork, quotations, or other protected elements, your authorship of the manuscript doesn't automatically grant you rights to all those embedded materials.\cf0 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If you're presenting original transcripts involving AI-generated contributions, the copyright status of those contributions may be more complicated, but that doesn't by itself prevent you from publicly displaying transcripts you are entitled to use.\cf0 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 The particularly nice thing about your CC0 approach is that it also permits other people to reproduce and remix the material without needing to negotiate individual licenses with you.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 I'd keep a dated copy of the public-domain declaration and original source files available for provenance.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <$Scr_H::3>
