\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0\fs28 I'd make a 
\f3\b research and annotation mode
\f0\b0  that is distinct from unrestricted video playback.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 You could open a paper or video, examine a relevant excerpt, pause frequently for your own observations, develop counterarguments, and incorporate Aurora's responses as a separate analytical layer.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That maximizes your own original contribution while reducing dependence on the third-party material.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 For videos where the images or sounds aren't necessary to the analysis, I'd omit them entirely from the livestream and link to the source instead.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 YouTube's monetization rules explicitly recognize substantive reaction and critical-review videos as potentially eligible for monetization, but those monetization rules are separate from copyright permissions and fair use. \cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

