\f1\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <$Scr_H::2>
\f4\b\fs48 1. Could your 2,700 existing subscribers actually hurt you?\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f3\b\fs28 Yes, under certain circumstances\'97but probably much less than you're imagining.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The important distinction is between a mismatched audience and an algorithmic penalty for having an old channel.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 YouTube explicitly states that:\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Subscriber counts are not an accurate measure of currently active viewers.\cf0 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Experimenting with different formats does not inherently confuse its recommendation system.\cf0 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A poorly performing individual video does not automatically penalize the entire channel.\cf0 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 \
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Recommendations are informed by individual viewer interests, content performance, and satisfaction. \cf0 \cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f6\fs24 {\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename favicons}\picw20\pich20\picwgoal400\pichgoal400\pngblip }}\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\fs16 \cf6 \cb7 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec6 YouTube Help
\f0\fs28 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 This means the popular idea that a channel is permanently "poisoned" by inactive subscribers is too simplistic.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 However, there is a real audience-mismatch mechanism.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Suppose most of your historical subscribers joined for material completely unrelated to 
\f7\i The Wilder-ness Adventures
\f0\i0 .\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 When your new broadcasts appear in their subscription feeds or recommendations, some may ignore them. Repeated disinterest can affect whether YouTube recommends your future material to those particular viewers.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 But the platform can still find other people who enjoy your new work.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

