\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0\fs28 Before deciding anything permanent, inspect 
\f3\b YouTube Studio \uc0\u8594  Analytics \u8594  Audience
\f0\b0 . Look at unique viewers, returning viewers, and activity over the last 90 days. These will tell you much more than the subscriber count alone.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Then publish an introduction and several actual broadcasts.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 My suggested decision window is approximately four to six streams, accompanied by a few independently packaged clips or videos.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 If the new material starts reaching interested viewers, whether subscribers or not, keep the channel.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 If you see persistent audience mismatch, poor discovery, and little response from existing subscribers, a new channel becomes worth testing\'97but don't attribute weak performance solely to the old channel without evidence.\cf0 \cb1 \
