\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 For an initial test, I'd try 720p at 30 frames per second if the computer or upload connection is constrained. If it handles your screen sharing, AI tools, webcam, and audio comfortably, you can try 1080p at 30 frames per second.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 You don't need 60 FPS to watch a person discussing theoretical physics or working on a manuscript.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 And because your work may involve lengthy AI conversations or reading dense text, I'd prioritize clear audio and legible documents over cinematic video quality.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 In OBS, watch for dropped frames, encoding overload, and rendering lag. If either streaming reliability or your ordinary working environment suffers, simplify the production rather than pushing the hardware harder.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

