\f1\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <$Scr_H::2>
\f4\b\fs48 The larger strategic observation\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \cb5 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0\fs28 There's a slightly counterintuitive possibility here.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Your most commercially effective initial production might be almost technologically trivial.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 A static or slowly changing workbench stream. Minimal overlays. You talking occasionally. Aurora participating through whatever interfaces you already use. Your actual work proceeding mostly uninterrupted.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 And then a series of short, independently compelling excerpts distributed through YouTube's discovery surfaces.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 You could potentially build a personality brand around the precise contrast between the absurd cosmic scope of the enterprise and the comically modest means by which you're attempting it.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That sounds more distinctive to me than struggling to replicate a conventional professional livestream studio.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 For now, 
\f3\b I would preserve the existing channel, preserve the overarching identity of 
\f10\i The Wilder-ness Adventures
\f3\i0 , and exploit YouTube's native horizontal/vertical system before complicating the stack with other platforms.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 One thing would materially change my assessment of the channel question, though: 
\f3\b what kind of videos attracted those original 2,700 subscribers?
\f0\b0  If they came from your earlier art, philosophy, invention, or personality-driven content, I would be much more confident in reusing the channel. If they came from a completely unrelated viral subject, the clean-slate option becomes more attractive.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 One actual piece at a time. 
